For what it's worth, as of 3am today for all 3.4.3 games on NAO:

There have been 216,689 deaths to date (ruling out quits/escapes).
676 have been 'poisoned by a (creature)'.
1109 have been 'poisoned by a (missile/trap)'.
A very small fraction are things like spellbooks and major demons.

That's 0.82% of all deaths that are from instapoison.
Creature poison, however, can typically be avoided with MC3, which is
typically available relatively easily either in the Mines or in the main
dungeon with an elven cloak.  So the 1109 that were from missile
weapons, poison spikes, etc. are the ones you really need poison
resistance for, and those are only 0.51% of all deaths.

Contrast this with the top 4 "killed-by-a" deaths:

killed by a soldier ant, 6275 deaths, 2.89% of total
killed by a jackal, 4979 deaths, 2.29% of total
killed by a water moccasin, 4746 deaths, 2.19%
killed by a wand, 4609 deaths, 2.12%
...
In all, 40 deaths in total are more common than being poison-instakilled
by a missile/trap, ...and bolts of fire, cold, and magic missile are
also represented in that list.

Conclusion?

You'll need poison resistance eventually, for sure, so don't neglect
your efforts to obtain it.  But early wishes should absolutely NOT be
burned on blessed tins of green dragon meat.  SDSM or GDSM will take you
much further, as the top 2 are preventable by good AC, the third by
staying out of the @#*$& fountains, and the fourth by reflection or
MR... and all of them are at least 4 times as likely to happen as being
instakilled by poison.

